      "source": [
        "# Digital Design - mod-21\n\n",
        "**Course:** digital-design\n\n",
        "Run the code cells below to practice.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Original state table (Moore machine):\nState | x=0 | x=1 | Output\n------|-----|-----|-------\n  A   |  B  |  C  |   0\n  B   |  D  |  A  |   0\n  C   |  D  |  A  |   0\n  D   |  E  |  C  |   1\n  E   |  E  |  C  |   1\n\nStep 1: Mark pairs with different outputs:\n  (A,D), (A,E), (B,D), (B,E), (C,D), (C,E) - marked (different outputs)\n\nStep 2: Check remaining pairs:\n  (A,B): x=0 gives (B,D)-marked \u2192 Mark (A,B)\n  (A,C): x=0 gives (B,D)-marked \u2192 Mark (A,C)\n  (B,C): x=0 gives (D,D)=same, x=1 gives (A,A)=same \u2192 EQUIVALENT!\n  (D,E): x=0 gives (E,E)=same, x=1 gives (C,C)=same \u2192 EQUIVALENT!\n\nResult: Merge B with C, merge D with E \u2192 3 states instead of 5!"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Transitions: S0\u2192S1\u2192S2\u2192S3\u2192S0\n\nBinary (2 FFs):       Gray (2 FFs):        One-Hot (4 FFs):\nS0=00  S1=01         S0=00  S1=01         S0=0001  S1=0010\nS2=10  S3=11         S2=11  S3=10         S2=0100  S3=1000\n\nBinary next-state:    Gray next-state:     One-Hot next-state:\nQ1_next = Q0         Q1_next = Q1 XOR Q0  state <= {state[2:0], state[3]}\nQ0_next = Q1'        Q0_next = Q1'        (simple rotation)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "always @(*) begin\n    case (state)\n        S0: next_state = ...;\n        S1: next_state = ...;\n        S2: next_state = ...;\n        default: next_state = S0;  // Return to known state\n    endcase\nend"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "wire state_error = (state == 4'b0000) |   // No bits set\n                   (state[3] + state[2] + state[1] + state[0] > 1); // Multiple bits"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Monolithic FSM (complex):\n  32 states, complex transitions, hard to verify\n\nDecomposed (simpler):\n  Controller FSM (8 states) \u2190\u2192 Datapath Counter (4-bit)\n  Each is simpler to design, verify, and maintain"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Inputs\n               \u2502\n    \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n    \u2502    \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25bc\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510         \u2502\n    \u2502    \u2502    FSM    \u2502         \u2502\n    \u2502    \u2502 Controller\u2502         \u2502\n    \u2502    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518         \u2502\n    \u2502     Control\u2502Signals      \u2502\n    \u2502          \u2502               \u2502\n    \u2502    \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25bc\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510         \u2502\n    \u2502    \u2502  Datapath \u2502         \u2502\n    \u2502    \u2502 (Registers,\u2502        \u2502\n    \u2502    \u2502  ALU, MUX) \u2502        \u2502\n    \u2502    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u252c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518         \u2502\n    \u2502    Status\u2502Flags          \u2502\n    \u2502    (zero,\u2502carry, etc.)   \u2502\n    \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518               \u2502\n               \u2502               \u2502\n               \u25bc               \u2502\n            Outputs            \u2502\n               \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Algorithm: Result = 0; repeat B times: Result = Result + A\n\nStates:\n  IDLE: Wait for start signal\n  ADD:  Add A to accumulator, decrement counter\n  DONE: Signal completion"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "module repeated_add_multiplier(\n    input  wire       clk,\n    input  wire       rst_n,\n    input  wire       start,\n    input  wire [3:0] A,\n    input  wire [3:0] B,\n    output reg  [7:0] product,\n    output reg        done\n);\n    localparam IDLE = 2'b00;\n    localparam ADD  = 2'b01;\n    localparam DONE_ST = 2'b10;\n    \n    reg [1:0] state, next_state;\n    reg [7:0] accumulator;\n    reg [3:0] counter;\n    \n    // State register\n    always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin\n        if (!rst_n)\n            state <= IDLE;\n        else\n            state <= next_state;\n    end\n    \n    // Next-state logic\n    always @(*) begin\n        case (state)\n            IDLE:    next_state = start ? ADD : IDLE;\n            ADD:     next_state = (counter == 4'd1) ? DONE_ST : ADD;\n            DONE_ST: next_state = IDLE;\n            default: next_state = IDLE;\n        endcase\n    end\n    \n    // Datapath\n    always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin\n        if (!rst_n) begin\n            accumulator <= 8'b0;\n            counter <= 4'b0;\n            product <= 8'b0;\n            done <= 1'b0;\n        end else begin\n            done <= 1'b0;\n            case (state)\n                IDLE: begin\n                    if (start) begin\n                        accumulator <= {4'b0, A};\n                        counter <= B;\n                    end\n                end\n                ADD: begin\n                    accumulator <= accumulator + {4'b0, A};\n                    counter <= counter - 4'b1;\n                end\n                DONE_ST: begin\n                    product <= accumulator;\n                    done <= 1'b1;\n                end\n            endcase\n        end\n    end\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
